um-gravity problems while preserving tested gravitational physics and producing discriminating predictions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0011"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4597961fa20bb6f66323db0f216fab769efb809e6079be95a2c892bc00fc20fb","title":"Does violation of tree-level partial-wave unitarity locate new degrees of freedom, or can an effective theory restore elastic unitarity internally before new physics becomes accessible? Is significant inelasticity a better diagnostic?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4523080919414f4cb7d29d9299283e61fda7f0c912de551b3b95450666e1820a","title":"Can adding a second non-perturbative term to Kähler uplift relax the compactification-volume bound, produce controlled metastable de Sitter vacua, and statistically favor small positive vacuum energy?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:45ef74aceef210d62a6384e200f077d1cdabaf7e7f313293da00366634d068e2","title":"Which AdS vacua of four-dimensional maximal gauged supergravity preserve N>2 supersymmetries, which gaugings support them, and what mass spectra and AdS supermultiplets realize their partial supersymmetry breaking?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:45186f3663485eefb63017fc79cce84c54f3d2996b63c97c062c09d299241a94","title":"How do Euclidean crossing symmetry and reflection positivity encode Lorentzian causality, and which constraints on low-twist operator interactions follow directly from the conformal bootstrap?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0019"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:458ed4d5fc312d9c0b1d7c764f6407d8cb3e8303c4d63c9a145222150c7cd691","title":"Which CSTB parameters and initial conditions permit a single nonsingular bounce leading toward radiation domination, with enough locked-era and subsequent evolution to address horizon, homogeneity, flatness, and singularity problems?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:45e8d4bad1843a6dea5af58bb310db151ce2480614ba98139f032602516e1cf6","title":"What does a background-subtracted Smarr relation require for regular backreacted anti-M2 configurations in CGLP, distinguishing smearing, localization, M5 polarization, extremality and finite temperature?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:459a501400bd831a1c4638f5a60153a660c19228793faf1c2be51c2297f68784","title":"Can an orientifolded chiral quiver at a singularity be embedded in a compact type-IIB model satisfying global brane constraints, with stabilized closed-string moduli, a tunable Minkowski/de Sitter vacuum and viable inflation in the same geometry?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0025"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:45061ceb132d557b4131f8bfab9c382a391a82f306f6c67619f32712c2b03e50","title":"Can a warped extra dimension supply the hierarchical relaxion decay constants and Higgs-dependent barriers needed for cosmological relaxation, while protecting the Higgs above the relaxion cutoff?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:45f13278ed379d64ac304a1b92a6f0a8a2763f909e9b8626da2a5850160f1410","title":"Does a string scalar potential near an infinite-distance singularity have the regularity needed for α-attractor inflation, in addition to the matching kinetic structure?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question: